./filename - runs a program or script from the current directory.

time - runs a command and reports its real, user and sys execution time.

read - takes input from the user and stores it in a variable.

${str:pos:len} - extracts a substring of length len starting at position pos.

${#str} - gives the length of the string.

gcc file.c -o name - compiles a C source file into an executable with the given name.

#include <stdio.h> - adds the standard input/output library for printf and scanf.

#include <string.h> - adds the string library for functions like strlen().

strlen() - returns the length of a string.
